["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"The Troubles Were Not a Religious War but a Zero-Sum Game of Demographic Anxiety Britain long ignored Northern Ireland&#x27;s internal demographic anxiety and economic imbalance, leaving the problem to the streets; in the summer of 1966, while Londoners cared only about the World Cup, violence in Ulster was about to spiral out of control. The Rest Is History The Rest Is History 697. The Troubles: Murder in Belfast (Part 1) The Troubles British politics Nationalism Religious conflict The 60s Paisley The Troubles\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-restishistory-北爱冲突不是宗教战争-而是人口与经济的零和博弈/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/4d082c6220b28920-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:26:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Rest Is History</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>The Troubles Were Not a Religious War but a Zero-Sum Game of Demographic Anxiety</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Britain long ignored Northern Ireland&#x27;s internal demographic anxiety and economic imbalance, leaving the problem to the streets; in the summer of 1966, while Londoners cared only about the World Cup, violence in Ulster was about to spiral out of control.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">The Troubles</span><span class=\"tag\">British politics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"TSMC Trucks Half-Finished Wafers: The Secret Weapon of AI Capacity TSMC exploits over 90% tool overlap between N5 and N7 to truck wafers half-made at its Tainan fab to Taichung for finishing, freeing up AI capacity during the N5-to-N3 transition. The foundation of the AI boom is a fleet of ordinary trucks. Asianometry Asianometry How TSMC Uses Old Fabs to Make New Chips TSMC Chip Capacity Advanced Packaging AI Compute Semiconductor Manufacturing Cross-Node Utilization cross-node utilization gate-all-around (GAA) back end of the line (BEOL) CoWoS FOUP\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-asianometry-台积电用货车把旧厂改造成-ai-新产能/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/0b270b942de95cf3-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">15:47</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>TSMC Trucks Half-Finished Wafers: The Secret Weapon of AI Capacity</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">TSMC exploits over 90% tool overlap between N5 and N7 to truck wafers half-made at its Tainan fab to Taichung for finishing, freeing up AI capacity during the N5-to-N3 transition. The foundation of the AI boom is a fleet of ordinary trucks.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">TSMC</span><span class=\"tag\">Chip Capacity</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Distillation Is a Gray Area, but Zhang Yiming Says It Can Only Approach, Never Surpass Distillation violates user agreements but may not constitute infringement — a gray area nobody discusses publicly. Zhang Yiming refused to let ByteDance distill, on the grounds that it can only approach a rival, never surpass it, and the cost is that people inside the organization taking uncertain paths get neither resources nor recognition. 晚点聊 LateTalk 晚点聊 179: 蒸馏风暴：一场无人公开谈论的技术竞赛 Distillation Large Models ByteDance Anthropic Post-training distillation reasoning model agent trajectory multi-teacher distillation behavior fingerprint\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-latetalk-蒸馏是灰色地带-但张一鸣说它只能逼近不能超越/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/5fa229ca57235ef6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"晚\"><span class=\"dur\">49:33</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">晚点聊 LateTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>Distillation Is a Gray Area, but Zhang Yiming Says It Can Only Approach, Never Surpass</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Distillation violates user agreements but may not constitute infringement — a gray area nobody discusses publicly. Zhang Yiming refused to let ByteDance distill, on the grounds that it can only approach a rival, never surpass it, and the cost is that people inside the organization taking uncertain paths get neither resources nor recognition.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Distillation</span><span class=\"tag\">Large Models</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Anti-vaccine sentiment is nothing new: Jenner&#x27;s own book is full of people cursing him This episode shows the anti-vaccine movement is as old as vaccines; phage SPO1 drives its transcriptional temporal switch through liquid-liquid phase separation condensates; ancient smallpox DNA from South America confirms transmission by European colonisers; and declining reading plus AI-generated text threaten discernment. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1349: Smallpox and mummies phage vaccines smallpox phase separation anti-vaccine transcriptional regulation liquid-liquid phase separation (LLPS) intrinsically disordered region (IDR) biomolecular condensate RNA polymerase holoenzyme vaccinia virus factory synonymous substitution rate\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-twiv-反疫苗古已有之-噬菌体凝聚体是转录调控核心/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">2:03:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>Anti-vaccine sentiment is nothing new: Jenner&#x27;s own book is full of people cursing him</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">This episode shows the anti-vaccine movement is as old as vaccines; phage SPO1 drives its transcriptional temporal switch through liquid-liquid phase separation condensates; ancient smallpox DNA from South America confirms transmission by European colonisers; and declining reading plus AI-generated text threaten discernment.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">phage</span><span class=\"tag\">vaccines</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"The Roman Empire Wasn&#x27;t Held Up by Its Legions, but by the Enslaved Rome&#x27;s administration, army, households, workshops and mines ran almost entirely on enslaved people; after Carthage fell in 146 BC slavery became the engine of the economy, and once Augustus stopped expanding, it reproduced itself through childbirth. The Ancients The Ancients How Slavery Built the Roman Empire Roman history slavery Roman Empire ancient economy gender and class manumission verna servus poenae dispensator freedmen Pax Romana\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-ancients-罗马帝国是奴隶制的产物-无奴隶则无帝国/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7ffc0e03b96daabb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:07:26</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Ancients</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>The Roman Empire Wasn&#x27;t Held Up by Its Legions, but by the Enslaved</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Rome&#x27;s administration, army, households, workshops and mines ran almost entirely on enslaved people; after Carthage fell in 146 BC slavery became the engine of the economy, and once Augustus stopped expanding, it reproduced itself through childbirth.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Roman history</span><span class=\"tag\">slavery</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The US Isn&#x27;t Rescuing the Yen for Japan — It&#x27;s Rescuing Its Own Trillion in Treasuries The US intervened in the yen for the first time in 28 years, officially to help an ally; the real calculation is preventing Japan from dumping $1 trillion of Treasuries to defend its currency — which would push up America&#x27;s own borrowing costs. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle The Hidden Risk in the US-Japan Yen Rescue Treasuries Yen FX Intervention US Treasury Interest Rates Carry Trade carry trade forward premium puzzle Cakeism Treasury Convenience Yield\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-15-patrickboyle-美国救日元不是为日本-是为自家万亿美债/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2eb71149af422d0e-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">31:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0815</span></div>\n<h2>The US Isn&#x27;t Rescuing the Yen for Japan — It&#x27;s Rescuing Its Own Trillion in Treasuries</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The US intervened in the yen for the first time in 28 years, officially to help an ally; the real calculation is preventing Japan from dumping $1 trillion of Treasuries to defend its currency — which would push up America&#x27;s own borrowing costs.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Treasuries</span><span class=\"tag\">Yen</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Executive Order Says Vaccines Are Like Soda, Splits MMR Into More Shots: Every Sentence Is a Lie In the &quot;gold standard&quot; executive order, every sentence is called a lie: splitting MMR into more shots, vaccines as soda, Merck refusing — and the new CDC director will face a loyalty test. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1348: Clinical update with Dr. Daniel Griffin Vaccine policy MMR Outbreak data Parasites Long COVID Wastewater surveillance MMR ACIP lyophilized PICO sterile insect technique RIG\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-15-twiv-行政令里的谎言-拆mmr与汽水比喻都是伪科学/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">55:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0815</span></div>\n<h2>Executive Order Says Vaccines Are Like Soda, Splits MMR Into More Shots: Every Sentence Is a Lie</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In the &quot;gold standard&quot; executive order, every sentence is called a lie: splitting MMR into more shots, vaccines as soda, Merck refusing — and the new CDC director will face a loyalty test.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Vaccine policy</span><span class=\"tag\">MMR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Antibiotic Bowel Prep Before Colon Cancer Surgery May Be Selecting for the Bacteria That Drive Recurrence Antibiotic bowel prep before colon cancer surgery is meant to prevent infection; but the resistant bacteria in the guts of patients who recur shrug it off, and on the day of surgery their total bacterial load is 23 times that of non-recurring patients. The prep may be doing the selecting for future recurrence. This Week in Microbiology This Week in Microbiology 361: Bacteria and Colon Cancer Recurrence Colorectal cancer Gut microbiome Antibiotic resistance Bowel prep Collagenase Bacteriophage bowel prep collagenase type IV pilus MAT protein\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-thisweekinmicr-大肠癌手术前的抗生素清肠-可能恰好在替促癌细菌做筛选/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/0b2f5ae26988f1a6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">53:14</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Microbiology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>Antibiotic Bowel Prep Before Colon Cancer Surgery May Be Selecting for the Bacteria That Drive Recurrence</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Antibiotic bowel prep before colon cancer surgery is meant to prevent infection; but the resistant bacteria in the guts of patients who recur shrug it off, and on the day of surgery their total bacterial load is 23 times that of non-recurring patients. The prep may be doing the selecting for future recurrence.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Colorectal cancer</span><span class=\"tag\">Gut microbiome</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Fed Was Not Born Precise: What It Should Do Was Still Being Figured Out in the 1970s Before the 1970s, even Fed chairs could not say clearly what the Fed was for, and presidents simply ordered rate cuts to protect jobs. Volcker pushed rates above 20% to fight inflation head-on, and in doing so built the modern template: the chair watches only inflation and unemployment. 忽左忽右 忽左忽右 492 刘怡、于杰谈保罗·沃尔克与现代美联储制度的形成 Federal Reserve Inflation Dollar hegemony Bretton Woods Plaza Accord Monetary policy Triffin dilemma Bancor Eurodollar market Volcker shock\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-cn2aa250-美联储不是天生精密-它该干什么到1970年代还在摸索/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cb6acd126210dffb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"忽\"><span class=\"dur\">1:17:43</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">忽左忽右</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>The Fed Was Not Born Precise: What It Should Do Was Still Being Figured Out in the 1970s</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Before the 1970s, even Fed chairs could not say clearly what the Fed was for, and presidents simply ordered rate cuts to protect jobs. Volcker pushed rates above 20% to fight inflation head-on, and in doing so built the modern template: the chair watches only inflation and unemployment.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Federal Reserve</span><span class=\"tag\">Inflation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\" data-hay=\"The Antidote to Picky-Eating Anxiety: No Judgment, No Rewards, and Dessert Is Just Another Food A child&#x27;s relationship with food doesn&#x27;t hinge on whether they ate a particular thing, but on whether the parent sorts foods into good and bad, uses dessert as a reward, and allows themselves to feed according to the child&#x27;s real needs; the earlier a picky-eating signal is caught, the easier it is to change. Raising Good Humans Raising Good Humans Picky Eating &amp; Food Guilt with Jennifer Anderson Child feeding Picky eating Food anxiety Parent-child communication Body image Feeding psychology embodied independence hyper-palatable foods PSAE\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-raisinggh-挑食焦虑的解药-不评判-不奖励-甜点也是普通食物/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/9372f4ec9923f201-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"R\"><span class=\"dur\">46:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Raising Good Humans</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>The Antidote to Picky-Eating Anxiety: No Judgment, No Rewards, and Dessert Is Just Another Food</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A child&#x27;s relationship with food doesn&#x27;t hinge on whether they ate a particular thing, but on whether the parent sorts foods into good and bad, uses dessert as a reward, and allows themselves to feed according to the child&#x27;s real needs; the earlier a picky-eating signal is caught, the easier it is to change.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Child feeding</span><span class=\"tag\">Picky eating</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Straight women&#x27;s dating pessimism isn&#x27;t melodrama — it&#x27;s political regression and economic dependence Sarah Jones argues that straight women&#x27;s awkwardness and pessimism about dating men is both a real feeling and a performance, and behind it lie political regression, economic dependence, and a complex reality reinforced by social media. The Gray Area with Sean Illing The Gray Area Why straight dating feels bleak heteropessimism gender politics dating culture women&#x27;s predicament social commentary heteropessimism hopeful pessimism\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-grayarea-异性恋悲观主义-直女困境的真实与表演/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/94d1e3cbb8f9e58a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">57:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Gray Area with Sean Illing</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>Straight women&#x27;s dating pessimism isn&#x27;t melodrama — it&#x27;s political regression and economic dependence</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Sarah Jones argues that straight women&#x27;s awkwardness and pessimism about dating men is both a real feeling and a performance, and behind it lie political regression, economic dependence, and a complex reality reinforced by social media.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">heteropessimism</span><span class=\"tag\">gender politics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"El Niño Is Not a Short-Term Shock but a Permanent Loss of Growth El Niño is not just a short-term weather shock; research shows it permanently depresses the economic growth trajectory, a single strong El Niño can cause trillions of dollars in losses within five years, and we have not adapted. Odd Lots Odd Lots A Historic El Niño Is Coming That Could Cost the World Trillions El Niño Climate economics Economic growth Global warming Adaptation ENSO / El Niño-Southern Oscillation Teleconnection RONI / Relative Oceanic Niño Index Level effect\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-oddlots-厄尔尼诺不是短期冲击-而是永久性增长损失/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">55:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>El Niño Is Not a Short-Term Shock but a Permanent Loss of Growth</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">El Niño is not just a short-term weather shock; research shows it permanently depresses the economic growth trajectory, a single strong El Niño can cause trillions of dollars in losses within five years, and we have not adapted.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">El Niño</span><span class=\"tag\">Climate economics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Lindy Runs DeepSeek Across the Board, and Its Founder Wants Chinese Models Banned Flo Crivello says DeepSeek is now the driver of Lindy&#x27;s entire agent chain, and at the same time he argues the whole industry should be banned from using it — because competitors will use it, so he has to, and he&#x27;d rather solve the prisoner&#x27;s dilemma by coordination. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution Lindy Teammate: Flo Crivello on Multiplayer Agents, Memory &amp; Why He&#x27;d Ban the Chinese Models He Uses agent memory context engineering inference cost Chinese models enterprise sales prompt optimization hydration context bucket centary tree TOON hypothesis driven retrieval per-user LoRA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-cogrev-lindy-全线跑在-deepseek-上-创始人主张封禁中国模型/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cde4d0762bd9b4a2-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">2:06:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>Lindy Runs DeepSeek Across the Board, and Its Founder Wants Chinese Models Banned</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Flo Crivello says DeepSeek is now the driver of Lindy&#x27;s entire agent chain, and at the same time he argues the whole industry should be banned from using it — because competitors will use it, so he has to, and he&#x27;d rather solve the prisoner&#x27;s dilemma by coordination.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>12</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">agent memory</span><span class=\"tag\">context engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"SK hynix&#x27;s Turnaround Wasn&#x27;t HBM Technology, It Was Customer Relationships SK hynix&#x27;s turnaround wasn&#x27;t a bet on HBM technology but a bet on customer relationships and long-term commitment; Samsung&#x27;s bet on PIM edge inference handed the sole-supplier position at the ChatGPT moment to its rival. Asianometry Asianometry SK hynix and the HBM Revolution Semiconductors HBM Memory Chips Korean Chaebols Advanced Packaging AI Compute HBM / High Bandwidth Memory TSV / Through Silicon Via TC-NCF / Thermal Compression with Non-Conductive Film MR-MUF / Mass Reflow Molded Underfill HBM-PIM / Processing-in-Memory ADR / American Depositary Receipt\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-asianometry-sk-hynix-靠-hbm-翻身-客户战略赢过周期/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/143ca5977a616036-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>SK hynix&#x27;s Turnaround Wasn&#x27;t HBM Technology, It Was Customer Relationships</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">SK hynix&#x27;s turnaround wasn&#x27;t a bet on HBM technology but a bet on customer relationships and long-term commitment; Samsung&#x27;s bet on PIM edge inference handed the sole-supplier position at the ChatGPT moment to its rival.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Semiconductors</span><span class=\"tag\">HBM</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"After AI Made Chess Boring, It Made Chess Better In the Stockfish era, players imitated a perfect engine and games turned dull; neural-network engines play aggressive, unconventional chess and have pushed human strength higher. No Priors No Priors What Chess.com Teaches US About Superhuman Capabilities, with CEO Erik Allebest Chess AI and human skill Private equity Community products Games Stockfish Leela Chess Zero mittens bot ELO secondary\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-nopriors-ai-让国际象棋变无聊后-又让它更好看了/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cdff3faf801808d4-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">46:07</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">No Priors</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>After AI Made Chess Boring, It Made Chess Better</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In the Stockfish era, players imitated a perfect engine and games turned dull; neural-network engines play aggressive, unconventional chess and have pushed human strength higher.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Chess</span><span class=\"tag\">AI and human skill</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"A single robot model matches fine-tuned specialists out of the box, and compositional generalization now has strong evidence A single robot model matches fine-tuned specialists out of the box, and can especially generalize compositionally to robot arms it has never seen — all of it resting on using prompts to tame low-quality heterogeneous data; the bottleneck is shifting to reliability, speed and physical distribution. Y Combinator Y Combinator Chelsea Finn: This is the State of the Art in Robotics Embodied AI Robot models Reinforcement learning Data processing Compositional generalization Deployment cadence compositional generalization subgoal image time-to-success RL post-training\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-ycsp-机器人单模型开箱追平微调专才-组合泛化已有强证据/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/04a76cf95c327656-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">58:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Y Combinator</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>A single robot model matches fine-tuned specialists out of the box, and compositional generalization now has strong evidence</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A single robot model matches fine-tuned specialists out of the box, and can especially generalize compositionally to robot arms it has never seen — all of it resting on using prompts to tame low-quality heterogeneous data; the bottleneck is shifting to reliability, speed and physical distribution.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Embodied AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Robot models</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"49ers Injuries Blamed on a Substation? The Dose Is Off by 40x, and the Data Doesn&#x27;t Fit Either The conspiracy theory claiming a substation&#x27;s electromagnetic waves caused the 49ers&#x27; injury plague gets debunked point by point by a radiation expert and an injury database: the dose is far below safety limits, the cited papers don&#x27;t qualify, the 2014 expansion was a different station, and the data shows they aren&#x27;t even the worst off. Science Vs Science Vs We Solve the 49ers Viral Conspiracy Theory NFL Injury Data EM Radiation Conspiracy Theory Fact-Check Oxidative Stress milligauss deep story\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-sciencevs-变电站不背这口锅-49人队伤病阴谋论被拆穿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a3282246c3202bd6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:01:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Science Vs</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>49ers Injuries Blamed on a Substation? The Dose Is Off by 40x, and the Data Doesn&#x27;t Fit Either</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The conspiracy theory claiming a substation&#x27;s electromagnetic waves caused the 49ers&#x27; injury plague gets debunked point by point by a radiation expert and an injury database: the dose is far below safety limits, the cited papers don&#x27;t qualify, the 2014 expansion was a different station, and the data shows they aren&#x27;t even the worst off.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">NFL</span><span class=\"tag\">Injury Data</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"TMS works for only half of depression patients: the field is stuck because it doesn&#x27;t know how it changes the brain TMS is already in the clinic but remains a black box; unclear mechanism keeps efficacy at 50%. Using intracranial electrodes in epilepsy patients to get neuronal ground truth, the next step is to grind out an EEG biomarker and turn treatment from guessing parameters into closed-loop optimization. From Our Neurons to Yours From Our Neurons to Yours Transcranial magnetic stimulation and the future of psychiatry | Corey Keller TMS Neuromodulation EEG biomarker Depression TMS / transcranial magnetic stimulation theta burst stimulation cortical excitability limbic system subgenual cingulate (sgACC)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-fromourneurons-tms-治抑郁只有五成有效-卡在不懂它怎么改变大脑/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/372ab8e78a5e10ef-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"F\"><span class=\"dur\">46:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">From Our Neurons to Yours</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>TMS works for only half of depression patients: the field is stuck because it doesn&#x27;t know how it changes the brain</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">TMS is already in the clinic but remains a black box; unclear mechanism keeps efficacy at 50%. Using intracranial electrodes in epilepsy patients to get neuronal ground truth, the next step is to grind out an EEG biomarker and turn treatment from guessing parameters into closed-loop optimization.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">TMS</span><span class=\"tag\">Neuromodulation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"Coffee Doesn&#x27;t Get You Drunk — It Built the Modern Commercial Intelligence Network Coffee first kept Sufis awake for prayer; it doesn&#x27;t intoxicate, it makes people talk, so coffeehouses became clearinghouses for commercial intelligence, and then reshaped the global economy through slave plantations and branding. Today&#x27;s arguments about the latte are still written inside this five-hundred-year history. In Our Time In Our Time Archive: Coffee Coffee Business history Colonialism Social networks Supply chain Espresso Sufis Levant Company Lloyd&#x27;s List Robusta Moka pot espresso\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-inourtime-咖啡因催生了近代商业情报网络与社交空间/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c3f143ddc011b622-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">56:52</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">In Our Time</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Coffee Doesn&#x27;t Get You Drunk — It Built the Modern Commercial Intelligence Network</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Coffee first kept Sufis awake for prayer; it doesn&#x27;t intoxicate, it makes people talk, so coffeehouses became clearinghouses for commercial intelligence, and then reshaped the global economy through slave plantations and branding. Today&#x27;s arguments about the latte are still written inside this five-hundred-year history.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>10</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Coffee</span><span class=\"tag\">Business history</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Women&#x27;s testosterone falls 1% a year; perimenopausal brain metabolism drops 20% Women should establish a hormone baseline in their 20s, when testosterone is already falling about 1% a year; oral contraceptives lower ovarian cancer risk while possibly shrinking the clitoris by up to 20%; perimenopausal brain glucose metabolism drops an average of 20%, and hot flashes are a disease signal, not a minor nuisance. Huberman Lab Huberman Lab Essentials: How to Optimize Female Hormone Health for Vitality &amp; Longevity | Dr. Sara Gottfried Female hormones Testosterone Perimenopause Oral contraceptives Brain metabolism CGM SHBG / sex hormone-binding globulin CGM / continuous glucose monitor PCOS / polycystic ovary syndrome FDG PET / fluorodeoxyglucose positron emission tomography HPA axis / hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis CAC / coronary artery calcium score\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-huberman-女性激素真相-睾酮流失与围绝经期脑代谢/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a1ac1c82ed5e5947-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"H\"><span class=\"dur\">38:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Huberman Lab</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Women&#x27;s testosterone falls 1% a year; perimenopausal brain metabolism drops 20%</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Women should establish a hormone baseline in their 20s, when testosterone is already falling about 1% a year; oral contraceptives lower ovarian cancer risk while possibly shrinking the clitoris by up to 20%; perimenopausal brain glucose metabolism drops an average of 20%, and hot flashes are a disease signal, not a minor nuisance.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Female hormones</span><span class=\"tag\">Testosterone</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Trucking Rates Are Spiking, and It Isn&#x27;t Because Demand Came Back — It&#x27;s Because Enforcement Cut Supply English-language proficiency enforcement, the crackdown on non-domiciled CDLs and a Supreme Court ruling on broker liability are draining capacity at the same time. What ended the three-year trough wasn&#x27;t a freight recovery — it was a structural raising of the barrier to entry. The next time demand surges, the market won&#x27;t be able to add supply as fast as it did during COVID. Odd Lots Odd Lots Trucking Is Booming Again, And Drivers Aren&#x27;t Happy About It Trucking Regulation Capacity squeeze Cyclicals Physical infrastructure Labor non-domiciled CDL ELD (electronic logging device) freight broker FMCSA safety rating spot vs contract rate owner operator\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-oddlots-这轮卡车运价上涨来自供给被砍-不是需求回来了/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">46:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Trucking Rates Are Spiking, and It Isn&#x27;t Because Demand Came Back — It&#x27;s Because Enforcement Cut Supply</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">English-language proficiency enforcement, the crackdown on non-domiciled CDLs and a Supreme Court ruling on broker liability are draining capacity at the same time. What ended the three-year trough wasn&#x27;t a freight recovery — it was a structural raising of the barrier to entry. The next time demand surges, the market won&#x27;t be able to add supply as fast as it did during COVID.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Trucking</span><span class=\"tag\">Regulation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"After Firing the Tupperware Queen, the Company Buried Her Book Brownie Wise turned Tupperware into an American household name with home-party sales, then was fired for outshining the inventor and had her records destroyed — not officially acknowledged until a park was named for her in 2016. Throughline Throughline The blatant betrayal that erased the Tupperware queen from history Sales revolution Women at work Brand history American business Organizational power subversive domesticity burp Wonder Bowl Jubilee\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-throughline-特百惠女王遭公然背叛-被美国历史抹去/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/6899c998b8f2c10a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">49:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Throughline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>After Firing the Tupperware Queen, the Company Buried Her Book</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Brownie Wise turned Tupperware into an American household name with home-party sales, then was fired for outshining the inventor and had her records destroyed — not officially acknowledged until a park was named for her in 2016.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Sales revolution</span><span class=\"tag\">Women at work</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"LLMs Industrialize the Scam, and SSO Becomes the Master Switch When forging interviews, monitoring inboxes and synthesizing voices cost close to nothing, anyone&#x27;s SSO account can be quietly taken over; who the bank makes eat the loss matters more than teaching users to spot phishing. Complex Systems Complex Systems LLMs and the economics of Evil, Inc., with Manish Goregaokar LLM Anti-fraud Money laundering Cybersecurity Social engineering Supply chain attack BEC / business email compromise money mule AML / anti-money laundering Regulation E desk name supply chain attack\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-complexsys-大模型把骗局工业化-单点登录成了总开关/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/03fbe8332bb0a87a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:02:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Complex Systems</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>LLMs Industrialize the Scam, and SSO Becomes the Master Switch</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">When forging interviews, monitoring inboxes and synthesizing voices cost close to nothing, anyone&#x27;s SSO account can be quietly taken over; who the bank makes eat the loss matters more than teaching users to spot phishing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">LLM</span><span class=\"tag\">Anti-fraud</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"The Romans knew their founding myth was false, and used it as a diplomatic tool Rome&#x27;s origin myth was not history carved in stone but a flexible narrative the Romans used to negotiate, absorb foreign peoples and digest civil war; the archaeological evidence even directly conflicts with the 753 BC founding date. The Ancients The Ancients Romulus &amp; Remus Roman history myth and politics archaeology Aeneas Romulus oral tradition Rex Pomerium Casa Romuli Lupa\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-ancients-罗马人清楚建城神话是虚构的-但照样当外交工具/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a9395e3e4c90e300-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">59:55</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Ancients</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>The Romans knew their founding myth was false, and used it as a diplomatic tool</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Rome&#x27;s origin myth was not history carved in stone but a flexible narrative the Romans used 